Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||03-03-2001||01:13 PM||||What would an 87 GT with unknown mileage be worth?<BR>The paint looks like it was put on with a power Wagner electric paint gun <BR>(I am exaggerating but it has sat for some time and is extremely dirty.) <BR>It has an Automatic transmission. I don't know if the air works. <BR>Body looks fair, some lower damage on the driver side.<BR>The interior is tan and could be salvaged. The seats are gone and would need replaced.<BR>The needle is missing on the Speedometer.  He had to jump start it and it took 3 tries before it would crank. It seemed to idle high 2000. The seller claims to have recently replaced the engine if this is true it looks like he did a fair job, all of the connections look ok. I pushed up on the EGR and it started to stall and the tube looked ok. I had called him a week ago and the cash price was $1800 and when I stopped in today it was $2200. After we started it and looked at it awhile I brought some of the problems to his attention and he came down to $1500. I didn’t take it for a ride because it was blocked in by the other cars on the lot.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jake_Dragon<BR>1985 2.5L Sport Coupe<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||5
